pack={'subtopic':sub,'spec':'9701','version':1,'note':note,'outline':'Use group position and established periodic trends to predict an untested element’s properties. For an unknown, combine shell count, outer electrons, atomic radius and reactions; every clue must agree with the proposed period, group and identity.','misconceptions':mis,'worked':worked,'items':items,'flashcards':[{'id':'fc1','kc':k1,'front':'What does chemical periodicity allow you to predict?','back':'Characteristic properties of an element from its position in a group and established trends.'},{'id':'fc2','kc':k2,'front':'How should an unknown element be deduced?','back':'Use the given physical and chemical properties together to infer its nature, possible Periodic Table position and identity.'}],'diagrams':[]}
